  "notes": "BQSTREAM is a RudderStack-unique stream connector; Segment handles BigQuery via warehouse sync only (no direct streaming insert equivalent). The BQStream producer uses the Google BigQuery streaming insert API (bigquery.Inserter.Put) to write GenericRecord maps directly to BigQuery tables. Each GenericRecord is a map[string]bigquery.Value where all event fields are flattened to top-level keys. The insertId field provides deduplication and is separated from row data by the Save() method. The producer supports both single-record and batch (array) inserts. Destination config requires projectId, datasetId, tableId, and GCP credentials. Timeout is configurable via common.Opts. No Segment payload comparison is possible."
